    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d294">

                <pb facs="0516" n="422" xml:id="pg422"/>

                <head>No. 294.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. von
                            Alvensleben to Mr. Bayard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Imperial German Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1887-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic">April</hi> 29, 1887</date>.
                        (Received April 29.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Secretary of State</hi>: I have the honor, in
                    obedience to instructions received, herewith to send you the reply of His
                    Majesty the Emperor and King to the congratulatory letter addressed to His
                    Majesty by the President of the United States on the occasion of the anniversary
                    of His Majesty’s birth. I also inclose a copy of this communication, which I
                    most respectfully beg you to transmit to its destination.</p>
                <p>Accept, Mr. Secretary of State, a renewed assurance of my most distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. V.
                    Alvensleben.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d294-a1.xml" xpointer="d294-a1"/>
